<title>FINLAND: CHINESE IN TALKS WITH FINNISH TECHNOLOGY FIRMS.</title>
<headline>CHINESE IN TALKS WITH FINNISH TECHNOLOGY FIRMS.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chinese Yunnan province is interested in Finnish technology know-how and is currently talking about cooperation with different Finnish companies, the Ministry of Agriculture and Forestry said on Friday.</p>
<p>A delegation led by the governor of Yunnan province talked with engineering group Rauma Oy, mining and metals group Outokumpu Oy and chemicals company Kemira Oy, it said.</p>
<p>According to the ministry, Yunnan province is keen on developing the area's forest industry and forest agriculture.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom, +358-9-680 50 240, news@reuters.fi</p>
